A||||4||fiero56||power accessory completion||||7||
Z||000000||fiero56||07-03-2000||09:29 PM||||Well, my big FieroStore box arrived today. Inside it contained: pair of power door lock switches, pair of power window switches, '88 driver side parking brake cable, parking brake equalizer, and rear deck release switch.<P>I am almost finished with the installation of PW, PL, and PM. I have the drivers door yet to complete(I didn't want to lose the ability of rolling down the window until completed). I removed the dash, and installed all wiring in factory locations, used all factory wiring harnesses, and the passenger door is completed. Power everything on it. This project is finally coming to a close(started gathering parts in April), should finish tommorrow.<P>Total cost, lets see:<BR>PM heads: around $60/pair(thanks Dave)<BR>PW motors: $20/pair with doors(mrfiero)<BR>PL solonoids: free(thanks Scott)<P>PM & PW wiring: free(compliments of Scott)<BR>PL wiring: about $20 from junkyard<P>PW switches: $26/pair<BR>PL switches: $10/pair<BR>PM switch: don't have one yet<P>I will be writing an article in the next week. ||||reg||7
Z||000001||87ECO5||07-03-2000||10:48 PM||||Way to go, Drew!  Glad to hear you saw this thing through to completion!  So, when are you coming over to install my power decklid release!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||TOM||07-04-2000||01:33 AM||||I have a power mirror switch if you still need one. I might even have the surround piece to mount the switches.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||07-06-2000||10:28 PM||||Well, it's almost official, I have yet to paint and install the door map pockets, and install a power mirror switch, but the power accessory installation was a sucess.<P>While I had the doors apart, I figured that it was a good time to fix the "problem" of the door glass sticking up 1/2" from the dew wipes when fully retracted. My door glass now goes all the way down. It takes 30 seconds to fix. At the bottom of the door is a rubber disk that the lower window track hits. I took out the disk on both doors. No problems yet, and the glass fully retracts. Figured I would let everyone in on this. It doens't look like any damage will ocurr because of the missing rubber stop.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||07-07-2000||10:33 AM||||Drew--If you can't find a p/mirror switch before I get another one (mine only works one way), you can have mine.  It's all black.  Maybe you can clean the contact or something and fix it?  I'll let you know when I get another mirror switch.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
